    rdfs:label "Evidence for Wood and Timber Dye Woods Brazil Wood used in Calico Cloth & Calico Printing: Andrew Ure, A Dictionary of Arts, Manufactures, and Mines (2nd ed., 1840; Project Gutenberg #44562), s.v. C D E F"@en ;
    <ontology/quoteText/#resource> "They are next rinsed in cold water, and steeped in water very faintly acidulated with sulphuric acid, during 4 hours, then rinsed, and dried. Preparation of Mordants.--1 gallon of boiling water; 2 pounds of alum; dissolve: 1 pound of acetate of lead; 4 ounces of sal-ammoniac; 1 of chalk; mix well together; after decomposition and subsidence, draw off clear. ..."@en ;
